{"success": true, "name": "arc-stream-review-lessons", "file": "references/session-output-shape-and-transfer-review.md", "content": "# Session review: invalid-grid feedback, unsupported transfer, and action discipline

In this instance, test dimensions were 21×13. The first guessed output was rejected as “not a valid ARC grid”; later candidate arrays appeared to have 21 rows and 13 values each, but continued to rely on unsupported stamping of the embedded 3/5 motif around every 8 marker. Demos were heterogeneous: some extended a small colored seed/object from isolated markers, while the last example replicated a multicolor stencil around marker locations. Their different colors and object geometry did not establish that the test's 8s select the seed copy operation.

Reusable lesson: after “invalid grid,” mechanically audit serialization (row count, every row width, palette and limits) before interpreting feedback. Then handle transformation semantics separately; satisfying the schema does not make a rule plausible. Use every fresh demo as immediate evidence before another action, and stop consulting overlapping references or calling no-op probes when they do not clarify the grid. Do not chain demo requests without reconciling the last pair. A previously identified session-specific reference already cautions that this task remained unsolved; no test transformation is established by this note.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1790545217/attempts/771c27e3136742b79bef1ff131c04e1e/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/arc-stream-review-lessons/references/session-output-shape-and-transfer-review.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "arc-grid-solving", "file": "references/output-shape-audit.md", "content": "# Output shape audit after invalid-grid feedback

When demos show different output and input dimensions, establish the output geometry separately from the cell-content rule. Never presume that output preserves input dimensions or infer the shape from a salient portion of the test. Record each pair's exact input/output dimensions and test the proposed structural mapping against all examples.

Before submission, mechanically check row count, each row's width, and legal cell values. If evaluator feedback says the grid was not a valid ARC grid, treat that first as a dimension/serialization failure—not semantic evidence—and repair the structural output shape before another submission. In strict action tasks, make this audit before emitting the JSON object.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1790545217/attempts/771c27e3136742b79bef1ff131c04e1e/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/arc-grid-solving/references/output-shape-audit.md"}
